# What a checkout's .env.local holds. Copy it: cp .env.example .env.local
# md seeds .env.local into every md worktree from the main checkout, so fill the main checkout's
# copy once. Each variable is read in exactly one src/config.ts (lint/no-raw-process-env.grit).
# Never put a secret, a token or a real learner's data here: this file is committed.

# --- Read today ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres for packages/store's integration tests (*.int.test.ts). Read by
# packages/store/src/config.ts, and by `make migrate` and `make pgtap`. `make db` creates both
# databases on Postgres.app's 17 server (prod's major version) at port 5433; its 18 server on 5432
# belongs to other projects.
# Records live in Supabase Postgres in prod
# (jadwigo-platform/decisions/2026-10-26-jadwigo-s-records-live-in-supabase-postgres-in-place-of-dynamodb);
# locally and in CI they run on plain Postgres, never Docker.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5433/jadwigo_test
# psql, createdb and pg_prove in the Makefile reach the same server.
PGPORT=5433

# The parent's sign-in on `make dev`: jadwigo-dev's Supabase Auth (apps/web/src/config.ts). With
# the URL or the key empty, the app has no sign-in. JW_SUPABASE_KEY is jadwigo-dev's publishable
# key, which every browser that opens the app holds, so it is public. It stays empty here only
# because gitleaks flags its shape: copy it from the Supabase dashboard, project jadwigo-dev, Project
# Settings → API Keys (dl-e8ov.2.82). JW_SUPABASE_PROVIDERS lists the buttons shown, comma separated:
# the providers infra/supabase-auth/dev.json turns on (dl-e8ov.2.8, dl-e8ov.2.58).
JW_SUPABASE_URL=https://jweuvslwntdimuwcvlzq.supabase.co
JW_SUPABASE_KEY=
JW_SUPABASE_PROVIDERS=google,facebook

# --- Decided, read once packages/bank is built (dl-n9fr.4) --------------------------------------

# Which bank createBank uses (packages/bank): fixture | api.
# david-learns/decisions/2026-10-24-the-question-bank-is-never-committed-to-the-jadwigo-repo:
# fixture is made-up question sets built by factories (every unit test); api is the bank through
# POST /api/v1/question-searches. local and remote are served by jadwigo-bank, not built here.
# JADWIGO_BANK=fixture

# The local bank folder, outside this repo. It is the bank's own private repo
# (jadwigo-question-bank/decisions/2026-10-27-the-question-bank-lives-in-its-own-pr), once
# dl-n9fr.15 moves the pages there. Until then, the dl-brain checkout.
# JADWIGO_BANK_DIR=~/projects/dl-brain

# --- Not set here -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ports: WEB_PORT (apps/web) and API_PORT (apps/api, and the web dev server's /api proxy).
# .md/repo.toml declares them with the main checkout's numbers, 5173 and 8730; `md run dev` exports
# each worktree's own, and tools/src/ports.ts fails when one is unset inside a worktree.
# docs/runbooks/local-dev.md has the one command.

# Supabase secrets: never here or in .env.local. `make db-push`, `db-reset ENV=dev` and `db-role`
# read ~/.config/jadwigo/supabase.env (mode 600), outside every checkout (docs/runbooks/migrations.md).

# AWS: sessions never hold prod credentials, and unit tests fail when any AWS_* credential is set
# (packages/testing/src/unit-setup.ts). The owner's profiles stay in ~/.aws.
